# Tic-Tac-Toe AI Agent

A Python implementation of a simple **AI agent that learns to play Tic-Tac-Toe using Q-learning**.

The agent trains by playing thousands of games through self-play and against a random opponent. After training, the user can play against the trained AI.

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates the basic concepts of **Reinforcement Learning** using the Tic-Tac-Toe game.

The AI learns which moves are more valuable by receiving rewards for winning, ties, and losing. It stores the learned values of different board states and moves in a Q-table.

The project covers:

* Game board representation
* Available move detection
* Win detection
* Tie detection
* Q-learning
* Exploration and exploitation
* AI training
* AI evaluation
* Human vs AI gameplay

