## Main Functions

### `new_board()`

Creates a new empty Tic-Tac-Toe board.

### `print_board(board)`

Displays the current board in a readable 3×3 format.

### `available_moves(board)`

Returns the positions that are still available.

### `check_winner(board, player)`

Checks whether the specified player has completed a winning combination.

### `is_tie(board)`

Checks whether the game has ended in a tie.

### `train(agent)`

Trains the Q-learning agent through repeated games.

### `evaluate(agent)`

Tests the trained agent against a random player.

### `main()`

Controls the complete gameplay process, including training, evaluation, and human-vs-AI gameplay.

